{
  "id": "LUK.24",
  "number": "24",
  "bookId": "LUK",
  "reference": "Luke 24",
  "verseCount": 42,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "24",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "LUK 24"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "24",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And behold, two of them were going that very day to a village named Emmaus, which was threescore furlongs from Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And they communed with each other of all these things which had happened. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, while they communed and questioned together, that Jesus himself drew near, and went with them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But their eyes were holden that they should not know him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said unto them, What communications are these that ye have one with another, as ye walk? And they stood still, looking sad. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And one of them, named Cleopas, answering said unto him, Dost thou alone sojourn in Jerusalem and not know the things which are come to pass there in these days? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said unto them, What things? And they said unto him, The things concerning Jesus the Nazarene, who was a prophet mighty in deed and word before God and all the people: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and how the chief priests and our rulers delivered him up to be condemned to death, and crucified him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But we hoped that it was he who should redeem Israel. Yea and besides all this, it is now the third day since these things came to pass. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moreover certain women of our company amazed us, having been early at the tomb; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and when they found not his body, they came, saying, that they had also seen a vision of angels, who said that he was alive. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And certain of them that were with us went to the tomb, and found it even so as the women had said: but him they saw not. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said unto them, O foolish men, and slow of heart to believe in all that the prophets have spoken! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Behooved it not the Christ to suffer these things, and to enter into his glory? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And beginning from Moses and from all the prophets, he interpreted to them in all the scriptures the things concerning himself. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And they drew nigh unto the village, whither they were going: and he made as though he would go further. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And they constrained him, saying, Abide with us; for it is toward evening, and the day is now far spent. And he went in to abide with them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, when he had sat down with them to meat, he took the bread and blessed; and breaking ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " he gave to them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And their eyes were opened, and they knew him; and he vanished out of their sight. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And they said one to another, Was not our heart burning within us, while he spake to us in the way, while he opened to us the scriptures? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And they rose up that very hour, and returned to Jerusalem, and found the eleven gathered together, and them that were with them, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.33"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "34",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:34"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "34",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "saying, The Lord is risen indeed, and hath appeared to Simon. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.34"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "35",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:35"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "35",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And they rehearsed the things ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.35"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " in the way, and how he was known of them in the breaking of the bread.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.35"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "35",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:35"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "35",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.35"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "36",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:36"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "36",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And as they spake these things, he himself stood in the midst of them, and saith unto them, Peace ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.36",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.36"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " unto you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.36",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.36"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "37",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:37"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "37",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But they were terrified and affrighted, and supposed that they beheld a spirit. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.37",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.37"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "38",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:38"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "38",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said unto them, Why are ye troubled? and wherefore do questionings arise in your heart? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.38",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.38"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "39",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:39"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "39",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "See my hands and my feet, that it is I myself: handle me, and see; for a spirit hath not flesh and bones, as ye behold me having. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.39",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.39"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "40",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:40"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "40",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when he had said this, he showed them his hands and his feet. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.40",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.40"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "41",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:41"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "41",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And while they still disbelieved for joy, and wondered, he said unto them, Have ye here anything to eat? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.41",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.41"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "42",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:42"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "42",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And they gave him a piece of a broiled fish. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.42",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.42"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "43",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:43"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "43",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he took it, and ate before them.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.43",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.43"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "43",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:43"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "43",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.43",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.43"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "44",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:44"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "44",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said unto them, These are my words which I spake unto you, while I was yet with you, that all things must needs be fulfilled, which are written in the law of Moses, and the prophets, and the psalms, concerning me. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.44",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.44"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "45",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:45"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "45",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then opened he their mind, that they might understand the scriptures; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.45",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.45"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "46",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:46"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "46",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and he said unto them, Thus it is written, that the Christ should suffer, and rise again from the dead the third day; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.46",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.46"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "47",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:47"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "47",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and that repentance and remission of sins should be preached in his name unto all the nations, beginning from Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.47",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.47"
            ]
          }
